cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Inexact and Accelerated Proximal Point Algorithms
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying report, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyễn
    given-names: Hoàng Tú
  - family-names: Bùi
    given-names: Công Hoàng Vũ
  - family-names: Huỳnh
    given-names: Trung Kiên
  - family-names: Nguyễn
    given-names: Ngọc Diễm Quỳnh
abstract: >-
  A report and numerical study of accelerated proximal point algorithms whose
  subproblems are solved only approximately. Two notions of inexactness are
  analysed, each giving a different accumulated-error term, and the experiments
  check the resulting convergence bounds numerically rather than illustrating
  them: the bounds are tested at every outer iteration, and the decay rate of
  each error component is measured against the order the theory predicts.
keywords:
  - convex optimization
  - proximal point algorithm
  - Nesterov acceleration
  - estimate sequences
  - inexact subproblem solves
